This is a project which will help me learn cheat sheets and practice text manipulation in NeoVim simultaneously
This game is simply to make the right vertical split match the text of the left vertical split

This is played by:
1. feeding the game a target file
1. The game augments this in memory
1. Another window is open where the augmented data is shown
1. The user then uses NeoVim to make the second window match the first
1. The user then runs a "check" command to verify that the files match

I though this would be a good idea to make memorization not as boring,
and hopefully that being able to identify and correct small mistakes would
reinforce learning better that a rote method.


There are currently two run modes -g and -c

First the user is expected to start a game
This can be done by :Golf -g /path/to/file.txt
This mode sets the game, augments the file, and then runs a diff check

Presumably after some changes have been made, the user can run a check
This can be done by :Golf -c
This will run the check logic and remark the target file with x's and checks
There is no true "termination" of the game, this is just a fun widget for now

